Warning; 
Danger;
Some enemies are immune to your poison until you get your physical poisons at 51 i believe.
You will notice a SIGNIFICANT DROP IN DAMAGE WHEN YOUR POSIONS DONT WORK

Not yet tested Weaponswitch on Target-Type -Makro as workaround for this stupid patch:

#showtooltipp
/startattack
/equipmh [type:Undead/Elemental/Giant/Mechanical nomhimbue:Dissolvent_Poison] YourDissolventMHDagger;
/equipoh [type:Undead/Elemental/Giant/Mechanical noohimbue:Dissolvent_Poison] YourDissolventOHDAgger;
/equipmh [notype:Undead/Elemental/Giant/Mechanical mhimbue:Dissolvent_Poison] YourInstantMHDagger;
/equipoh [notype:Undead/Elemental/Giant/Mechanical ohimbue:Dissolvent_Poison] YourInstantOHDAgger;

Regards to [Super]CleveRoidMacro (https://github.com/jrc13245/SuperCleveRoidMacros/wiki/)

For supercleveroid I've been using this, and it's a pretty good one button - can add backstab if daggers, and even set a conditional for position behind to only use if you are behind the target - I use this for swords
#showtooltip
/startattack 
/cast [nomybuff:"Slice and Dice" combo:=1] Slice and Dice;
/cast [nomybuff:envenom combo:=1]Envenom;
/cast [usable:"Surprise Attack"]Surprise Attack;
/cast [combo:>1] Eviscerate
/cast [mypower:>40]Sinister Strike
